content.text:
[
  {
    "requirement": "Shipped work on a blockchain or protocol component, not just a design doc",
    "score": 10,
    "rationale": "This is the rarest thing on the list and the closest the role has to a hard filter; without it, everything else is a maybe."
  },
  {
    "requirement": "A decade or more owning architecture decisions that shipped",
    "score": 9,
    "rationale": "The role is largely unsupervised technically, so we're leaning on track record instead of a formal vetting process we don't have time to build."
  },
  {
    "requirement": "Recent, hands-on coding ability in Rust or a comparable systems language",
    "score": 8,
    "rationale": "The posting frames this as a strong preference rather than a hard line, but candidates who can't credibly write code themselves will struggle to review the hardest parts of the system."
  },
  {
    "requirement": "Experience running production infrastructure on a major cloud provider at real scale",
    "score": 8,
    "rationale": "They're already on GCP and don't sound eager to migrate, so depth there matters more than breadth across multiple clouds."
  },
  {
    "requirement": "Distributed systems experience at a scale where naive debugging stops working",
    "score": 8,
    "rationale": "A platform aiming at a global audience will hit exactly this wall; someone who hasn't been there before will learn it the hard way, in production."
  },
  {
    "requirement": "Practical, hands-on security and threat-modeling experience",
    "score": 7,
    "rationale": "The posting is explicit about wanting security built in from day one, not bolted on later, which argues for someone who has actually done that before."
  },
  {
    "requirement": "A track record of shipping, not just designing",
    "score": 7,
    "rationale": "Given the founding-equity structure, the team needs proof this person finishes things, not just architects them well on a whiteboard."
  },
  {
    "requirement": "Experience leading people through genuinely ambiguous situations",
    "score": 6,
    "rationale": "The posting is unusually candid that the role starts underspecified; someone who needs a fully-scoped brief before moving will stall out."
  },
  {
    "requirement": "Strong written communication for an async, distributed team",
    "score": 6,
    "rationale": "With everyone remote and the CTO only part-time at first, most coordination will happen in writing rather than meetings."
  },
  {
    "requirement": "Comfort being the technical voice in investor conversations",
    "score": 5,
    "rationale": "It's explicitly called out as part of the job, but it's a secondary skill relative to the core technical bar \u2014 nice to already have, teachable if not."
  }
]

